Falsifies `memory_regions::proofs::a_split_keeps_every_count_exact_and_under_its_ceiling`.

The defect: every split takes a sixteenth of its parent's ceilings, not of its root's. It reads as
the same rule, and it is for a child of the root, but a grandchild then lives under a 256th of the
root's ceilings and a deep job shrinks to nothing.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(same_ceilings(s.ceilings, ceilings_of(1,
run.root_ceilings)), "a split child's ceilings are not its root's share")`, on a split from the
child.

